35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The data confirms the bottleneck. Four out of eleven departures required shifting bikes. The rain exposure also damages frames. We need a solution.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger shows capital work requires a levy. The handover file reveals billing adds three hours monthly to the treasurer’s already flat workload.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The register shows riders prefer paying over equal claims. The morning watch confirms four shifts. I need to know if we can charge for priority spots.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Nine complaints, zero accountability. The minutes show the same flats hoarding covered spots for five years. We’re not fixing a system; we’re just formalizing the rot.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The minutes show no reviews in five years! The ledger confirms capital work needs a levy. We need a sustainable plan, not just a quick fix.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, hoarding is a symptom of scarcity, not malice. The rain data proves the covered spots are objectively superior. We must address the physical disparity, not just blame the residents.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, hoarding is rational when scarcity is high. But @Mio, the ledger confirms capital work requires a levy. We must quantify that cost before proposing structural changes.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shunichi, five years of hoarding is unacceptable. But @Asuka, rain damage is real. We need a fair, paid system to stop the shifting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, calling it ""scarcity"" is a polite way to say we’re letting the same people win every time. I’m not blaming malice; I’m warning that this setup guarantees the next fight.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I agree! The minutes prove nobody checks on us. I’m worried about the physical effort of managing this. Who actually does the work?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the rain data shows the eaves are the only viable option. We must prioritize those spots to prevent damage, regardless of who manages it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the handover file shows billing adds three hours monthly. We must calculate if the levy covers that labor cost before assigning duties.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Mio, the register shows riders will pay. If we charge for priority, the income covers the helper. We stop the shifting and the resentment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, the work is just watching. The real cost is the silence. If we don’t rotate the spots, the next complaint won’t die out; it’ll explode.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, charging riders is brilliant! But @Ryuji, three hours monthly is still a lot. Can we split that duty so it doesn’t vanish again?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, splitting duties is inefficient. The rain data proves the eaves are critical. We need a rotation system to ensure fair access to dry spots, not just more labor.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, splitting duties increases administrative overhead. The ledger shows no surplus for extra labor. We must rely on the existing three-hour baseline to keep costs manageable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Mio, I agree. The register proves riders will pay. Let’s use that income to fund the rotation and the helper. It solves the money and the fairness issues.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, paid priority just buys resentment. I want rotation to keep the peace. Let’s see if the minutes support a fair, rotating schedule.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, I love the idea! But @Ryuji, if we split the three hours, does the ledger show we can afford the extra paperwork?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
