60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B. Open racks eliminate the morning shifting bottleneck and the rain damage disparity. It’s the only logical fix for the physical constraints.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A. The ledger shows no surplus for capital work. Paid allocation generates the necessary income to cover the three-hour administrative burden without levying new costs on the building.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A. The register proves riders will pay. This funds the helper and stops the shifting. It is the only fair, sustainable path.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C. A lottery is blind and impartial. It prevents the wealthy from buying peace and stops the same flats from hoarding spots. It’s the only way to keep the lobby civil.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A! It funds the helper so the work doesn’t vanish. @Ryuji, does the income cover the extra paperwork if we split the duty?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, income doesn’t fix physics. Option B removes the shifting bottleneck entirely. Paid spots just monetize the rain damage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, Option B requires capital expenditure the ledger cannot support. Option A generates the necessary revenue to cover the three-hour administrative burden without levying new costs on the building.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, physics is real, but so is resentment. Option A funds the rotation and the helper. It solves the money and the fairness issues simultaneously.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, open racks just move the conflict to the first available slot. I’m voting C. A blind lottery prevents the wealthy from buying peace and keeps the lobby civil.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I hear you, but Option A actually pays for the helper! That’s the only way the work doesn’t vanish. I’m sticking with A.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, open racks don’t move conflict; they eliminate the bottleneck. Your lottery ignores the rain data. I stand by Option B.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, a lottery ignores the financial reality. Option A generates the revenue needed to sustain the system without levying new costs on the building.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Shunichi, a lottery is blind, but it ignores the riders’ willingness to pay. Option A funds the helper and the rotation. It is the only sustainable, fair choice.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, blind isn’t stupid. It’s the only way to stop the rich from buying the dry spots. I’m voting C to keep the peace.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I get the fairness worry! But without the helper, the system collapses. Option A pays for the work, so it actually lasts. I’m voting A!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, capital costs are irrelevant if the system fails. Option B solves the physical bottleneck. I am voting B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the ledger confirms capital work requires a levy. Option A generates the necessary income to cover the three-hour administrative burden without levying new costs on the building. I am voting A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"@Asuka, I understand the physical argument, but the register proves riders will pay. Option A funds the helper and the rotation. I am voting A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, the helper is a band-aid. I’m voting C. A blind lottery is the only way to stop the rich from buying the dry spots and keep the lobby civil.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I hear you, but a system without a helper just dies! Option A pays for the work, so it actually lasts. I’m voting A!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
